note ---- the arena (no table capacities; Drake 2026-11-11, OMEGESE 9.6; port of omc.om's a_* unit) -------
note Every ng table whose size depends on the input is a region of one pool, ar_m (16777216 words, 128 MiB):
note the payload (front input or ΩIR binary), the output, ΩIR global data and globals, the front's names,
note long names, functions, calls, blocks, breaks, continues, inline edges, value-depth cells, call-graph
note order, om2 diag site records and the front-ir lowering tables, and a64's global addresses. A region
note starts empty and doubles when an index reaches its group's capacity (ar_need); when the moved copies
note do not fit, the arena is compacted and the group grows in place to the largest size that fits, so the
note only capacity left is the arena itself. Running out of it is a refusal of the stage that asked
note (front error 14, a reader's LIMIT class 23, a writer's `ng: arena full`) with an ng-use record on
note stderr naming every group and the words it held (ar_rec). What bounds the arena: ng has no run-time
note growth (no heap, decision 24); one pool is at most 16777216 elements (OMEGESE 9.4), so 128 MiB of
note ulong words; its pages are never resident until touched. It lives in ir.om because every ng tool is
note composed with ir.om first (ng, ngrun, ngrand and the oracles), so each has the same arena.
note Regions (ar_defs): ar_rb base word, ar_rw words held, ar_rg group, ar_rm words per group index (0: a
note byte region, eight bytes to a word). Groups: ar_gc capacity, ar_gp highest index asked for, plus 1.
note ar_top words handed out, ar_wst words left behind by moves, ar_fl 1 once the arena was full, ar_nr
note regions defined, ar_wb staging bytes of read and write. Element i of a word region R is
note `get ar_m add get ar_rb R i` (a uchar or uint region keeps one element per word, read through a
note conversion and written by ar_pc / ar_pu); an index below the group capacity holds by construction
note at every such access (the count that bounds it was asked of ar_need first). Where an index comes from
note input it is checked (ar_g, ar_p): past its region is a fault of ng itself and traps 3, never another
note region's word.
global ar_m ulong 16777216
global ar_rb ulong 160
global ar_rw ulong 160
global ar_rg ulong 160
global ar_rm ulong 160
global ar_gc ulong 48
global ar_gp ulong 48
global ar_top ulong 1
global ar_wst ulong 1
global ar_fl ulong 1
global ar_nr ulong 1
global ar_ord ulong 160
global ar_np ulong 160
global ar_wb uchar 65536
global ar_rbuf uchar 4096
global ar_rc ulong 1
note ar_inl: bytes read into region 0 by ar_rdin (also while it reads, so a full arena's record shows them)
global ar_inl ulong 1
note ar_oc: bytes of region 1 (the output) written so far, for the record
global ar_oc ulong 1
note ar_gl (generated with ar_defs): the group labels of the ng-use record, each ended by a space
text ar_gl "in out gdat site names namehash long longhash fns fnhash calls blocks breaks conts inledge depth kahnfn kahncall lnames lnamehash lstack lsnap laq lca irglob a64glob a64val a64live a64call a64code a64fix "

note ar_def: region r is in group g with m words per group index (0: a byte region)
fn ar_def r ulong g ulong m ulong to void
put ar_rg r g
put ar_rm r m
if ge r get ar_nr 0
put ar_nr 0 add r 1
end
end

note ar_words: the words region r takes at group capacity c
fn ar_words r ulong c ulong to ulong
m = get ar_rm r
if eq m 0
ret shr add c 7 3
end
ret mul c m
end

note ar_move: room in region r for group capacity c. The last region handed out grows in place; any other
note moves to the top with its words copied, and the words it leaves behind are counted in ar_wst. Words
note past ar_top were never handed out and are 0. ar_need has checked that the group fits first, so the two
note full tests below are never met (they stay as a defence: 1 is returned and nothing moves).
fn ar_move r ulong c ulong to ulong
w = ar_words r c
o = get ar_rw r
if le w o
ret 0
end
b = get ar_rb r
t = get ar_top 0
if and ne o 0 eq add b o t
if gt sub w o sub len ar_m t
ret 1
end
put ar_top 0 add b w
put ar_rw r w
ret 0
end
if gt w sub len ar_m t
ret 1
end
ar_copy t b o
put ar_wst 0 add get ar_wst 0 o
put ar_rb r t
put ar_rw r w
put ar_top 0 add t w
ret 0
end

note ar_copy: words s .. s + n - 1 to d .. d + n - 1 in ascending order (d above s + n, or d below s)
fn ar_copy d ulong s ulong n ulong to void
i = ulong 0
while lt i n bound 16777217
put ar_m add d i get ar_m add s i
i = add i 1
end
end

note ar_copyd: words s .. s + n - 1 to d .. d + n - 1 in descending order (d above s: a slide up)
fn ar_copyd d ulong s ulong n ulong to void
i = n
while gt i 0 bound 16777217
i = sub i 1
put ar_m add d i get ar_m add s i
end
end

note ar_clear: words a .. b - 1 become 0
fn ar_clear a ulong b ulong to void
i = a
while lt i b bound 16777217
put ar_m i 0
i = add i 1
end
end

note ar_need: group g is about to use index n; 0 when it may, 1 when the arena has no room (ar_fl set,
note nothing changed but a compaction). Below the group's capacity nothing happens; at or above it every
note region of the group grows to twice the capacity (at least n + 1, at least 64), moving to the top when
note not there already. When the moved copies do not fit in the free words, the arena is compacted (the
note words moved regions left behind are reclaimed) and the group grows in place (ar_relayout), to twice
note when that fits, else to the largest capacity that does (ar_gfit). So a table is refused only when
note the live tables with its group grown by one entry no longer fit in the arena.
fn ar_need g ulong n ulong to ulong
if eq get ar_nr 0 0
ar_defs
end
if ge n get ar_gp g
put ar_gp g add n 1
end
c = get ar_gc g
if lt n c
ret 0
end
c = shl c 1
if le c n
c = add n 1
end
if lt c 64
c = ulong 64
end
if gt ar_gneed g c sub len ar_m get ar_top 0
ar_compact
if gt ar_gextra g c sub len ar_m get ar_top 0
c = ar_gfit g n c
if eq c 0
put ar_fl 0 1
ret 1
end
end
ar_relayout g c
put ar_gc g c
ret 0
end
r = ulong 0
while lt r get ar_nr 0 bound 161
if eq get ar_rg r g
if ne ar_move r c 0
put ar_fl 0 1
ret 1
end
end
r = add r 1
end
put ar_gc g c
ret 0
end

note ar_gneed: the words group g's regions take at capacity c, counted as if every one of them moved
fn ar_gneed g ulong c ulong to ulong
s = ulong 0
r = ulong 0
while lt r get ar_nr 0 bound 161
if eq get ar_rg r g
s = add s ar_words r c
end
r = add r 1
end
ret s
end

note ar_gextra: the words group g's regions need beyond the words they hold, at capacity c
fn ar_gextra g ulong c ulong to ulong
s = ulong 0
r = ulong 0
while lt r get ar_nr 0 bound 161
if eq get ar_rg r g
w = ar_words r c
if gt w get ar_rw r
s = add s sub w get ar_rw r
end
end
r = add r 1
end
ret s
end

note ar_gfit: when doubling does not fit, the capacity group g grows to in place: the largest in n + 1 .. hi whose
note growth takes at most half the free words (binary search; the need grows with the capacity), so the other
note groups keep room to grow (omc's a_gfit takes all of it; ng's a64 stage grows several groups per function),
note else n + 1 when that alone fits in the free words, else 0 (the arena is full)
fn ar_gfit g ulong n ulong hi ulong to ulong
f = sub len ar_m get ar_top 0
lo = add n 1
if gt ar_gextra g lo f
ret 0
end
h = shr f 1
if gt ar_gextra g lo h
ret lo
end
while gt sub hi lo 1 bound 64
mid = add lo shr sub hi lo 1
if gt ar_gextra g mid h
hi = mid
else
lo = mid
end
end
ret lo
end

note ar_lowest: index + 1 of the region holding words with the lowest base above lb (any base when any is
note false), or 0 when none is left
fn ar_lowest any bool lb ulong to ulong
best = ulong 0
bb = ulong 0
r = ulong 0
while lt r get ar_nr 0 bound 161
if ne get ar_rw r 0
b = get ar_rb r
if or not any gt b lb
if or eq best 0 lt b bb
best = add r 1
bb = b
end
end
end
r = add r 1
end
ret best
end

note ar_compact: slide every region down over the words moved regions left behind, in order of base, so
note the free words are one run at the top again; the words above the new top become 0. Region 0, the
note payload, has base 0 and stays there.
fn ar_compact to void
t = get ar_top 0
pos = ulong 0
lb = ulong 0
any = false
k = ulong 0
while lt k 161 bound 162
best = ar_lowest any lb
if eq best 0
k = ulong 161
else
r = sub best 1
b = get ar_rb r
w = get ar_rw r
if ne b pos
ar_copy pos b w
put ar_rb r pos
end
pos = add pos w
lb = b
any = true
k = add k 1
end
end
ar_clear pos t
put ar_top 0 pos
put ar_wst 0 0
end

note ar_relayout: after ar_compact (regions contiguous from word 0 in order of base), give group g's
note regions their words at capacity c in place: new places in the same order, every region at or above
note its old place, moved from the top down (ar_copyd), each new tail zeroed. A region of g that holds no
note words yet goes at the top.
fn ar_relayout g ulong c ulong to void
k = ulong 0
lb = ulong 0
any = false
go = true
while go bound 162
best = ar_lowest any lb
if eq best 0
go = false
else
r = sub best 1
put ar_ord k r
k = add k 1
lb = get ar_rb r
any = true
end
end
r = ulong 0
while lt r get ar_nr 0 bound 161
if and eq get ar_rg r g eq get ar_rw r 0
put ar_ord k r
k = add k 1
end
r = add r 1
end
pos = ulong 0
i = ulong 0
while lt i k bound 161
r = get ar_ord i
put ar_np i pos
w = get ar_rw r
if eq get ar_rg r g
w = ar_words r c
end
pos = add pos w
i = add i 1
end
i = k
while gt i 0 bound 161
i = sub i 1
r = get ar_ord i
np = get ar_np i
b = get ar_rb r
w = get ar_rw r
if and ne np b ne w 0
ar_copyd np b w
end
put ar_rb r np
if eq get ar_rg r g
nw = ar_words r c
if gt nw w
ar_clear add np w add np nw
put ar_rw r nw
end
end
end
put ar_top 0 pos
end

note ar_zero: the first k words of region r become 0
fn ar_zero r ulong k ulong to void
b = get ar_rb r
ar_clear b add b k
end

note ar_gzero: every word of every region of group g becomes 0 (a hash table about to be rebuilt)
fn ar_gzero g ulong to void
r = ulong 0
while lt r get ar_nr 0 bound 161
if eq get ar_rg r g
ar_zero r get ar_rw r
end
r = add r 1
end
end

note ar_hash: the b-bit multiplicative hash of w (2^64 divided by the golden ratio, odd)
fn ar_hash w ulong b ulong to ulong
ret shr mul w 11400714819323198485 sub 64 b
end

note ar_oob: an index past its region is a fault of ng itself, never an input's: trap 3 (the pool check on
note ar_rb at index 160 + i, always past its 160), as an index past a fixed pool trapped
fn ar_oob i ulong to void
z = get ar_rb add 160 i
end

note ar_g / ar_p: element i of word region r, read or written, checked against the region (indices that
note come from input). ar_pc / ar_pu: element i of a uchar / uint region written (index by construction).
fn ar_g r ulong i ulong to ulong
if ge i get ar_rw r
ar_oob i
end
ret get ar_m add get ar_rb r i
end
fn ar_p r ulong i ulong v ulong to void
if ge i get ar_rw r
ar_oob i
end
put ar_m add get ar_rb r i v
end
note ar_w / ar_c / ar_u: element i of a ulong / uchar / uint region read through a call: the form of a line
note whose inline reads do not fit omc's 16-register expression pool (index by construction, unchecked)
fn ar_w r ulong i ulong to ulong
ret get ar_m add get ar_rb r i
end
fn ar_c r ulong i ulong to uchar
ret uchar get ar_m add get ar_rb r i
end
fn ar_u r ulong i ulong to uint
ret uint get ar_m add get ar_rb r i
end
fn ar_pw r ulong i ulong v ulong to void
put ar_m add get ar_rb r i v
end
fn ar_pc r ulong i ulong v uchar to void
put ar_m add get ar_rb r i ulong v
end
fn ar_pu r ulong i ulong v uint to void
put ar_m add get ar_rb r i ulong v
end

note ar_ib: byte i of region 0, the payload. It is the first region placed, so it starts at word 0. Past its
note words the byte is 0, as the zero pool past the input was.
fn ar_ib i ulong to uchar
x = shr i 3
if ge x get ar_rw 0
ret 0
end
ret uchar and shr get ar_m x shl and i 7 3 255
end

note ar_bg: byte i of byte region r (0 past its words)
fn ar_bg r ulong i ulong to uchar
x = shr i 3
if ge x get ar_rw r
ret 0
end
y = get ar_m add get ar_rb r x
ret uchar and shr y shl and i 7 3 255
end

note ar_bp: byte i of byte region r becomes v. Every writer asked ar_need for the byte first, so the index is in
note the region by construction and is not checked here (the omc owner measured 11 to 13% for checking every
note arena access; checks stay where an index comes from input: ar_g, ar_p, ar_ib)
fn ar_bp r ulong i ulong v uchar to void
x = add get ar_rb r shr i 3
s = shl and i 7 3
y = and get ar_m x not shl ulong 255 s
put ar_m x or y shl ulong v s
end

note ar_stage: bytes p .. p + c - 1 of the byte region at word b into ar_wb from 0 (c at most 65536). Bytes up to a
note word boundary one at a time, then each whole word read once for its 8 bytes, then the last bytes
fn ar_stage b ulong p ulong c ulong to void
i = ulong 0
while and lt i c ne and add p i 7 0 bound 8
ar_stage1 b add p i i
i = add i 1
end
while le add i 8 c bound 8193
y = get ar_m add b shr add p i 3
put ar_wb i uchar and y 255
put ar_wb add i 1 uchar and shr y 8 255
put ar_wb add i 2 uchar and shr y 16 255
put ar_wb add i 3 uchar and shr y 24 255
put ar_wb add i 4 uchar and shr y 32 255
put ar_wb add i 5 uchar and shr y 40 255
put ar_wb add i 6 uchar and shr y 48 255
put ar_wb add i 7 uchar shr y 56
i = add i 8
end
while lt i c bound 8
ar_stage1 b add p i i
i = add i 1
end
end

note ar_stage1: byte x of the byte region at word b into ar_wb at i
fn ar_stage1 b ulong x ulong i ulong to void
y = get ar_m add b shr x 3
put ar_wb i uchar and shr y shl and x 7 3 255
end

note ar_out: write bytes p .. e - 1 of byte region r to fd, 65536 at a time through ar_wb: 1 when every
note byte was written, 0 when a write returned 0 or less
fn ar_out fd ulong r ulong p ulong e ulong to ulong
b = get ar_rb r
q0 = p
while lt q0 e bound 2049
c = sub e q0
if gt c 65536
c = ulong 65536
end
ar_stage b q0 c
q = ulong 0
while lt q c bound 65537
n = write int fd ar_wb q sub c q
if le n 0
ret 0
end
q = add q ulong n
end
q0 = add q0 c
end
ret 1
end

note ar_rdin: all of fd into region 0 (the payload), eight bytes to a word from word 0, before any other
note region is placed: 0 done, 1 a read error, 2 the arena is full (ar_inl: the bytes read). The region
note then keeps the words the bytes fill and 8 more (zero): the input bytes are read inline past their end
note by at most that much (the tokenizers look one or two bytes ahead), and the next region starts after.
fn ar_rdin fd int to ulong
off = ulong 0
go = true
while go bound 134217729
n = read fd ar_wb 0 65536
if eq n 0
go = false
else
if lt n 0
put ar_inl 0 off
ret 1
end
c = ulong n
put ar_inl 0 add off c
if ne ar_need 0 add off c 0
ret 2
end
ar_pack off c
off = add off c
end
end
put ar_inl 0 off
w = add shr off 3 8
if ne ar_need 0 sub shl w 3 1 0
ret 2
end
put ar_rw 0 w
put ar_top 0 w
put ar_gc 0 shl w 3
ret 0
end

note ar_pack: the c bytes of ar_wb become payload bytes off .. off + c - 1 (their words are 0 until now). Bytes
note up to a word boundary one at a time, then whole words of 8 (one store each), then the last bytes (measured
note under qemu-aarch64 on a 14785-byte unit: 502253 guest instructions a byte at a time, 160761 this way)
fn ar_pack off ulong c ulong to void
i = ulong 0
while and lt i c ne and add off i 7 0 bound 8
ar_pack1 add off i get ar_wb i
i = add i 1
end
while le add i 8 c bound 8193
y = ulong get ar_wb i
y = or y shl ulong get ar_wb add i 1 8
y = or y shl ulong get ar_wb add i 2 16
y = or y shl ulong get ar_wb add i 3 24
y = or y shl ulong get ar_wb add i 4 32
y = or y shl ulong get ar_wb add i 5 40
y = or y shl ulong get ar_wb add i 6 48
y = or y shl ulong get ar_wb add i 7 56
put ar_m shr add off i 3 y
i = add i 8
end
while lt i c bound 8
ar_pack1 add off i get ar_wb i
i = add i 1
end
end

note ar_pack1: payload byte x becomes b (its word's other bytes are kept)
fn ar_pack1 x ulong b uchar to void
w = shr x 3
put ar_m w or get ar_m w shl ulong b shl and x 7 3
end

note ar_gwords: the words the regions of group g hold
fn ar_gwords g ulong to ulong
s = ulong 0
r = ulong 0
while lt r get ar_nr 0 bound 161
if eq get ar_rg r g
s = add s get ar_rw r
end
r = add r 1
end
ret s
end

note ar_gcount: what group g was asked to hold: the payload's and the output's bytes, else the highest index
note asked for, plus 1 (bytes for a byte group)
fn ar_gcount g ulong to ulong
if eq g 0
ret get ar_inl 0
end
if eq g 1
ret get ar_oc 0
end
ret get ar_gp g
end

note record writer: bytes into ar_rbuf (flushed to fd when near full)
fn ar_rb1 fd ulong b ulong to void
c = get ar_rc 0
if ge c 4000
w = write int fd ar_rbuf 0 c
c = ulong 0
end
put ar_rbuf c uchar b
put ar_rc 0 add c 1
end
fn ar_rn fd ulong v ulong to void
d = ulong 1
while le d div v 10 bound 20
d = mul d 10
end
x = v
while gt d 0 bound 21
ar_rb1 fd add 48 div x d
x = rem x d
d = div d 10
end
end
note ar_rs: the bytes "k=" of a key packed little-endian in w (n bytes)
fn ar_rs fd ulong w ulong n ulong to void
x = w
for i ulong n bound 8
ar_rb1 fd and x 255
x = shr x 8
end
end

note ar_rec: the ng-use record, one line to fd: ng-use 1 arena=A top=T waste=W full=F, then for each group
note LABEL=N/H, N what it was asked to hold (ar_gcount) and H the words it holds. A, T, W and H count 8-byte
note words of the arena; F is 1 when a stage was refused because the arena was full.
fn ar_rec fd ulong to void
put ar_rc 0 0
ar_rs fd 3539940853674764142 8
ar_rs fd 17277100355641632 7
ar_rn fd len ar_m
ar_rs fd 263879357472 5
ar_rn fd get ar_top 0
ar_rs fd 17281524405729056 7
ar_rn fd get ar_wst 0
ar_rs fd 67535885395488 6
ar_rn fd get ar_fl 0
g = ulong 0
p = ulong 0
while lt p len ar_gl bound 1024
ar_rb1 fd 32
while ne get ar_gl p 32 bound 16
ar_rb1 fd ulong get ar_gl p
p = add p 1
end
p = add p 1
ar_rb1 fd 61
ar_rn fd ar_gcount g
ar_rb1 fd 47
ar_rn fd ar_gwords g
g = add g 1
end
ar_rb1 fd 10
w = write int fd ar_rbuf 0 get ar_rc 0
put ar_rc 0 0
end

note ar_die: a stage with no refusal path of its own: `ng: arena full`, the record, exit 14
text ar_dmsg "ng: arena full\n"
fn ar_die to void
w = write 2 ar_dmsg 0 len ar_dmsg
ar_rec 2
exit int 14
end

